ations\nDarwin Day\nEarthstock\nDepartmental Resources\nAI & Technology Policy\nField Safety Equipment\nMore\n\u00d7\nSearch\nSearch\nCollege of Arts and SciencesDepartment of Ecology & Evolution\nHome\nAbout Us\nDepartment Leadership\nDiversity Statement\nFacilities\nGiving to E&E\nContact Us\nResearch\nResearch Areas\nFaculty Labs\nPublications\nPeople\nFaculty & Staff\nE&E Alumni\nJoin Us\nAcademic Programs\nAdmissions & Financial Support\nPh.D. Program\nPh.D. Admissions\nProgram Roadmap\nProgram Goals & Student Life\nTuition and Funding\nM.A. Program (Closed for 2027-2028)\nM.A. Admissions\nProgram Roadmap\nProgram Goals & Student Life\nTuition and Funding\nUndergraduate Programs\nEcology and Evolution Specialization\nEnvironmental Biology Specialization\nHuman Evolutionary Biology\nUndergraduate Resources\nEcoEvo Society\nUndergraduate Research Opportunities\nSpotlight\nAdvising\nNews & Events\nDepartment News\nDepartment Calendar\nEvents\nColloquium & Dissertations\nDarwin Day\nEarthstock\nDepartmental Resources\nAI & Technology Policy\nField Safety Equipment\nReaching New Heights in Ecology & Evolution\nOur graduate students are at the forefront of ecological and evolutionary discovery\nREAD MORE ABOUT OUR PROGRAMS\nSPOTLIGHT\nReference Genomes and Fossils Revise Bat Family Phylogeny and Biogeography: Uncover the origins of bats! Featured in Nature, it is a paper written by international scientists co-led by Professor Liliana M.\nD\u00e1valos. It is the first-ever reconstruction of the bat family tree.\nCALENDAR\nIN THE NEWS\nRead about our new faculty PRODiG+ Fellow Dr. Anna Thonis featured on IACS\nProfessors Robert Thacker and Elizabeth Watson secured more than $270K in funding\nfrom the NYS Department of Environmental Conservation to tackle invasive species and\nprotect local ecosystems.\nJoin us in congratulating Luis on his newly published paper: https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0169534726002156\nProfessor Watson recieved a grant award by the New York State Department of Environmental\nConservation. This will support three graduate student researchers in collaboration\nwith the Shinnecock Nation.\nDr. Yun Tao has been named one of Stony Brook University\u2019s inaugural Simons Empire\nFaculty Fellows\nUndergraduate Programs\nMA Program\nPhD Program\nProfessional Opportunities\nFooter\nDepartment of Ecology & Evolution\n650 Life Sciences Building | Stony Brook, NY 11794-5245\nPHONE: 631-632-8600 | FAX: 631-632-7626 | EMAIL: ecoevo_office@stonybrook.edu\nPrivacy Policy\nReporting Discrimination\nSexual Misconduct\nAccessibility Barrier\n\u00a9 2026 Stony Brook University\n\u00a9", "links": [["", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/"], ["College of Arts and Sciences", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/commcms/cas/"], ["Department of Ecology & Evolution", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/ecoevo/index.html"], ["", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/ecoevo/index.html"], ["About Us", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/ecoevo/about-us/index.html"], ["Department Leadership", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/ecoevo/about-us/leadership.html"], ["Diversity Statement", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/ecoevo/about-us/diversity-statement.html"], ["Facilities", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/ecoevo/about-us/facilities.html"], ["Giving to E&E", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/ecoevo/about-us/giving-to-ee.html"], ["Contact Us", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/ecoevo/about-us/contact-us.html"], ["Research", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/ecoevo/research/research-areas/index.html"], ["Research Areas", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/ecoevo/research/research-areas/index.html"], ["Faculty Labs", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/ecoevo/research/labs.html"], ["Publications", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/ecoevo/research/publications.html"], ["People", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/ecoevo/people/faculty/index.html"], ["Faculty & Staff", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/ecoevo/people/faculty/index.html"], ["E&E Alumni", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/ecoevo/people/alumni.html"], ["Join Us", "https